The OCI SDK response has no lifecycle-state
field or work-request handle, so create and
update are synchronous and settle through
read-after-write.
Pre-create reuse is limited to an exact unique
compartmentId plus displayName match.
Cooldown, display name, enabled state, and tag
maps reconcile in place. Every non-noop update
also carries the desired isEnabled value because
the live Autoscaling API rejects an otherwise
valid partial update when that field is omitted.
Compartment movement uses a separate provider
action that the published OSOK runtime does not
invoke, and resource/policy definitions remain
replacement-only.
Delete keeps the finalizer until
GetAutoScalingConfiguration returns NotFound.
The runtime has no Secret side effects.
end note
